cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite as below."
title: "AgroSense: Satellite-Based Crop Stress Classification and Smart Farming Decision Support for Pakistan Smallholder Agriculture"
authors:
  - family-names: Shahmeer
    given-names: Ali
  - family-names: Hassan
    given-names: Basit
    name-suffix: MS
  - family-names: Ghoto
    given-names: Kabir
    name-suffix: PhD
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
url: "https://github.com/ALI-SHAHMEER/agrosense-pakistan-crop-stress"
abstract: >
  Replication package for AgroSense: a spectral proxy crop-condition
  classification system using Sentinel-2 imagery collected via the Google
  Earth Engine API. The dataset contains 1,786 observations from 99
  georeferenced agricultural sampling locations (district/city-centroid
  buffers) across all four provinces of Pakistan, spanning 19 seasons
  (Kharif 2015-2024, Rabi 2016-2024). Class labels (Healthy / Stressed /
  Diseased) are derived from a vegetation health composite using NDVI, NDRE,
  and EVI via tertile split; these same indices are model input features
  (label circularity). Reported performance measures spectral proxy
  separability, not independently validated crop disease detection.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - precision agriculture
  - crop condition proxy classification
  - Sentinel-2
  - machine learning
  - Pakistan
  - Google Earth Engine
  - spectral indices
